This is a brilliant architectural and UX decision. Rendering a massive data grid in the browser for thousands of rows can cause lag, and if they are going to download the Excel file to review it anyway, the grid is completely redundant.
By removing the table, we can also **delete the backend API call that fetches the details**, which will make your application significantly faster!
Here are the precise steps to strip out the grid and replace it with a clean, professional "Download to Review" Call-To-Action (CTA) below your new Stepper.
### Step 1: Remove the Dead State Variables & Pagination Handlers
Since we don't have a table anymore, we don't need pagination states or the API call to fetch the grid data.
**FIND THIS BLOCK (Around line 112):**
```javascript
